'My proposed solution will leverage the largest YOLOv8 segmentation model, `yolov8x-seg.pt`, to better capture the intricate details of cell structures. The model will be trained for up to 50 epochs on high-resolution images (1024x1024), utilizing an early stopping mechanism with a patience of 10 epochs on the validation mask mAP50 to prevent overfitting and optimize training time. To enhance robustness to variations in cell orientation, I will enable data augmentations including 90-degree rotations and horizontal flips, which are suitable for microscopy data. For the final output, I will implement a careful post-processing step that sorts predicted instance masks by their confidence scores before merging them into a single `uint16` mask, ensuring that overlaps are resolved in favor of the most confident detections. The primary evaluation metric guiding this process will be the mean Average Precision for segmentation masks at an IoU threshold of 0.5 (mAP50), as reported on the validation set during training.'
